  "about": "A linear terminal read from the satellite (a u/v grid along its 1,020 m axis), the street frames and the Commons photographs: a main building with a north-west and a south-east concourse; five barrel vaults over the landside departures hall with a glazed valley between them; rows of skylights on the airside roof; a shallow pitched roof on each concourse; the departures kerb canopy; a jet bridge at every gate (OpenStreetMap). Facade in graphite and glass, roofs pale. Principles: departures above arrivals, gates on the airside, processing in the middle (Campbell, archgyan).",
